  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> and charge <math><mi>q</mi></math> has an initial velocity <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> . If an electric field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and magnetic field <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;act on the particle, its speed will double after a time",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EVFj1",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
